Summary of the most serious issues in this patch:
- `ctlv_attr_next()` error paths leave `cursor->attr` unchanged, so for-each loops can spin forever after a WARN.
- `ctlv_input_attr()` WARNs (and aliasing zeroes nest) when handed a `NULL`-attr nest, which is what an absent optional nest produces, so userspace can trigger the WARN.
- Pervasive redundant self-revalidation (about 5x per iteration) of a core-built index through `WARN_ON_ONCE`; dead if the core is correct, costly if not gated.
- Bisectability: Kconfig/Makefile are unreachable, `message.c` is not compiled until patch 11; `ctlv_message_index_free()` declared with no definition; `internal.h` and many struct fields are only used patches later.
- Cleanup: orphan trailing comment, unused includes, redundant *len reset, unused `CTLV_IN_*`/`ctlv_attr_s64`/bool API, menuconfig without children, no kernel-doc.
- Commit message claims request indexing that this patch does not implement.
